-- US-3125: colorways for 26 brands, from each brand's own catalogue.
--
-- The loop, rather than another hand-built pack. `brand_knowledge.source_url`
-- already holds each brand's homepage, so scripts/ops/brand-feed-probe.mjs asked
-- all 184 brands with no colorways which of them publish a readable catalogue,
-- and scripts/ops/shopify-brand-harvest.mjs read the 43 that do.
--
--   probed 184   feed 45   none 80   refused 15   skipped 40   error 4
--
-- -- THE RULE, STATED SO IT CAN BE ARGUED WITH ------------------------------
--
-- A colour is seeded when it appears on FIVE OR MORE products -- a house colour
-- rather than a one-off capsule.
--
-- A BRAND is seeded when it has at least 8 such colours AND no more than 35%%
-- of them are plain colour words. That second test is the one that matters: a
-- colorway earns its place by naming something the seller cannot name
-- themselves. "Spiced Chai" and "Maltese Blue" are knowledge; "Blue" is not,
-- and a table full of "Blue" looks covered while helping nobody.
--
-- CASE VARIANTS ARE ONE COLOURWAY. Several feeds carry "Black" and "BLACK" as
-- separate options; they are folded and the spelling that appears on the most
-- products wins.
--
-- -- WHAT WAS REFUSED, AND WHY ----------------------------------------------
--   antisocialsocialclub      6 colours -- too few recurring colours
--   bosca                    11 colours, 36%% plain -- palette is mostly plain colour words
--   denimtears               12 colours, 83%% plain -- palette is mostly plain colour words
--   gallerydept              16 colours, 62%% plain -- palette is mostly plain colour words
--   goorinbros               44 colours, 36%% plain -- palette is mostly plain colour words
--   hellstar                 10 colours, 90%% plain -- palette is mostly plain colour words
--   hudsonjeans               4 colours -- too few recurring colours
--   kangol                   47 colours, 45%% plain -- palette is mostly plain colour words
--   kith                      0 colours -- too few recurring colours
--   lucchese                  3 colours -- too few recurring colours
--   palace                    0 colours -- too few recurring colours
--   persol                    0 colours -- too few recurring colours
--   rebeccaminkoff            2 colours -- too few recurring colours
--   speedo                    0 colours -- too few recurring colours
--   spyder                    1 colours -- too few recurring colours
--   stetson                  33 colours, 45%% plain -- palette is mostly plain colour words
--
-- -- WHAT IS STILL NOT HERE -------------------------------------------------
--
-- NO HEX, for the reason 00732 gives: these feeds publish colour NAMES, not
-- values, and eyedropping a product photo is a guess wearing a fact's clothing.
--
-- NO SIZE CHARTS: a feed gives the size RUN and brand_size_charts holds BODY
-- MEASUREMENTS.
--
-- TAG ERAS, COUNTRY PATTERNS AND AUTHENTICATION TELLS are untouched for every
-- brand here. A product feed cannot say when a neck label changed.
--
-- TWO BRANDS THE HARVEST COULD NOT REACH: keen and toddsnyder answered 429 to
-- the end. That is a rate limit, not an absence, and the harvester throws on it
-- rather than recording an empty catalogue.

on conflict do nothing;

-- US-1108 self-record footer.
